, E.M. De La Cruz, H.N. Higgs, and T.D. Pollard. <year>1998</year>. Interactions of <italic>Acanthamoeba</italic> profilin with actin and nucleotides bound to actin. <source>Biochemistry.</source> <volume>37</volume>:<fpage>10871</fpage>&#x02013;10880.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9692980</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Wills, Z., L. Marr, K. Zinn, C.S. Goodman, and D. Van Vactor. <year>1999</year>. Profilin and the Abl tyrosine kinase are required for motor axon outgrowth in the <italic>Drosophila</italic> embryo. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>22</volume>:<fpage>291</fpage>&#x02013;299.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10069335</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Wolven, A.K., L.D. Belmont, N.M. Mahoney, S.C. Almo, and D.G. Drubin. <year>2000</year>. In vivo importance of actin nucleotide exchange catalyzed by profilin. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>150</volume>:<fpage>895</fpage>&#x02013;904.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10953013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, F.X., S.C. Lin, M. Morrison-Bogorad, and H.L. Yin. <year>1994</year>. Effects of thymosin beta 4 and thymosin beta 10 on actin structures in living cells. <source>Cell. Motil. Cytoskeleton.</source> <volume>27</volume>:<fpage>13</fpage>&#x02013;25.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8194107</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn1"><label>*</label><p>Abbreviations used in this paper: dAbi, <italic>Drosophila</italic> Abelson interacting protein&#x0003b; SEM, scanning electron microscopy.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>